I was surprised to discover that if you have a boxed slice of non-copy items you can't move out of it with a slice pattern:
```rust
#[derive(Debug)]
struct NonCopy(String);

fn f(s: Box<[NonCopy]>) -> Option<NonCopy> {
    match *s {
        [v] => Some(v),
        _ => None,
    }
}
```

messages.zh:
我很惊讶地发现，如果你有一个盒装的非拷贝项目切片，你不能用切片图案移出它：```rust
#[derive(Debug)]
struct NonCopy(String);

fn f(s: Box<[NonCopy]>) -> Option<NonCopy> {
    match *s {
        [v] => Some(v),
        _ => None,
    }
}
```

messages.en:
There’s also variadic slice patterns, which would require either drop in patterns or a new kind of drop tracking — but those could remain prohibited.
```rust
fn f(s: Box<[NonCopy]>) -> Option<NonCopy> {
    match *s {
        [v, ..] => Some(v),
        [] => None,
    }
}
```

