i am still not completely sure about this specific sentence in the description of yeet1 :
> From the programmer's perspective, the environment is guaranteed to return "halt", and the programmer can soundly rely on this when making safety proofs.

would the following code be considered correct modeling of the guarantees ?

[#t-libs > Pushing &#96;breakpoint&#96; over the finish line? @ 💬](#narrow/channel/219381-t-libs/topic/Pushing.20.60breakpoint.60.20over.20the.20finish.20line.3F/near/624086909)  to me indicates that i am correctly picturing it but i'd like to make sure.
```rs
// publicly non-constructible ZST. type level proof that we have resumed 
// from yeet1.
// the external program that caused the production of the ResumeToken
// takes full responsibility for all future uses of the token.
// because it is inhabited, the compiler will not immediately see the code
// adter it is produced as unreachable, but the programmer may 
// instead choose to mark following branches as  unreachable through 
// `unreacheable_after_resume`
#[derive(Clone, Copy)]
pub struct ResumeToken(());

impl ResumeToken {
    fn unreacheable_after_resume(self) -> ! {
        // SAFETY : the external tool that has resumed the program guarantees that 
        // this codepath will will never be reached
        unsafe { core::hint::unreachable_unchecked() }
    }
}

/// SAFETY : this is always safe to call, but unless otherwise specified,
/// it is not sound to resume a program after a call to yeet1.
///
/// Any specific call to yeet1 may specify a set of constraint under 
/// which it is sound to resume from it.
///
/// In that case, these constraints must include the fact that
/// the produced `ResumeToken` or any of its copies must never be used to call
/// `unreacheable_after_resume`
///
/// if any of the constraints are not satisfied, it is not sound to resume from
/// `yeet1`
pub fn yeet1() -> ResumeToken {
    /* compiler magic or syscalls idk */
    /* obviously blocks time traveling UB */
    ResumeToken(())
}
```

with use cases like

```rs
pub fn just_checking() {
    // it is always sound to resume from here, because we explicitly state there are no
    // constraints and immediately discard the produced `ResumeToken`.
    // still aborts if there is no debugger though
    yeet1();
}

pub fn totally_safe_fn() {
   // it is never sound to resume from here
   yeet1().unreacheable_after_resume();
}

use std::sync::OnceLock;
static CELL1: OnceLock<String> = OnceLock::new();
static CELL2: OnceLock<String> = OnceLock::new();

pub fn ensure_cells_are_populated() -> [&'static str;2] {
    // it is only sound to resume if CELL1 and CELL2 are populated
    let rt = yeet1();

    let Some(s1) = CELL1.get() else { rt.unreacheable_after_resume() };
    let Some(s2) = CELL2.get() else { rt.unreacheable_after_resume() };
    [&**s1, &**s2]
}


pub fn check_before_ffi_stuff() -> u64 {
    // it is only sound to resume if all the safety requirement for do_ffi_stuff to be called are fullfilled
    yeet1();

    unsafe { do_ffi_stuff(/* some_args */) }
}
```

