Even though I don't want subobject provenance really, I did think of an argument in favor of it in the recent allocator discussions. If you have a `ThinBox<dyn Foo>` (<https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/boxed/struct.ThinBox.html>, e.g. a box-like type which stores the metadata/vtable pointer in the same allocation as the data), it occurred to me that if the `dyn Foo` contains a `&mut self` function (which notably *not* the case for `Allocator`, which uses only interior mutability, which at least *seems* like a different situation to me), without subobject provenance it seems to me like the compiler would be forced to assume (in the absence of devirtualization/inlining) that any such function can overwrite the vtable pointer. For example:

```rs
pub trait Frob {
     fn frob(&mut self);
}
// Pointless struct wrapper since I don't think it's likely you
// would pass around a `&mut ThinBox<dyn T>` rather
// than a `&mut dyn T` in real code.
pub struct Something {
    frobber: ThinBox<dyn Frob>
    // other stuff...
}
pub fn twice_frob(x: &mut Something) {
    x.frobber.frob();
    // The first call might write to the vtable pointer,
    // so this call is forced to reload it from memory.
    x.frobber.frob();
}
```
That said, ThinBox's current implementation doesn't even use a struct (it uses opaque byte arrays and address arithmetic, as the version of this that uses `<T as Pointee>::Metadata` is invariant over T, rather than covariant like `Box<T>`). I don't know how relevant that actually is here, but I did feel that it's worth mentioning.

messages.zh:
虽然我确实不希望引入子对象来源，但在最近关于分配器的讨论中，我想到了一个支持它的论据。如果你有一个 `ThinBox<dyn Foo>`（<https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/boxed/struct.ThinBox.html>，例如一种类似 box 的类型，它将元数据/虚函数表指针与数据存储在同一次分配中），我突然想到：如果 `dyn Foo` 包含一个 `&mut self` 方法（值得注意的是，`Allocator` 并非如此，它只使用内部可变性；至少在我看来，这似乎是另一种情况），那么在没有子对象来源的情况下，编译器似乎就不得不假设：在没有去虚拟化或内联的情况下，任何这样的函数都可能覆写虚函数表指针。例如：

```rs
pub trait Frob {
     fn frob(&mut self);
}
// 没什么意义的结构体包装器，因为我不认为在实际代码中
// 你会传递一个 `&mut ThinBox<dyn T>`，而不是
// 一个 `&mut dyn T`。
pub struct Something {
    frobber: ThinBox<dyn Frob>
    // 其他内容……
}
pub fn twice_frob(x: &mut Something) {
    x.frobber.frob();
    // 第一次调用可能会写入虚函数表指针，
    // 因此这次调用必须从内存中重新加载它。
    x.frobber.frob();
}
```

话虽如此，ThinBox 当前的实现甚至没有使用结构体（它使用不透明的字节数组和地址运算，因为使用 `<T as Pointee>::Metadata` 的那个版本对 T 是不变的，而不像 `Box<T>` 那样是协变的）。我不知道这在这里到底有多大关系，但我觉得还是值得一提。

messages.en:
I didn't see it mentioned so it's probably not worth it, but just in case, we could have an explicit operation to restrict provenance (like in CHERI). We don't change any existing rules, so no additional UB. But we provide 2 new instrinsics: `fn restrict_provenance<T>(&T) -> &T` and `fn restrict_provenance_mut<T>(&mut T) -> &mut T` which return their argument but with provenance restricted to what the type says (maybe we need the same for raw pointers). The example from #**t-opsem>Vibes on subobject provenance@598416977**  would become:
```rust
fn f(b: &mut Buffered, g: fn(&mut [u8; N])) -> usize {
    b.i = 0;
    g(restrict_provenance_mut(&mut b.buf)); // was g(&mut b.buf)
    b.i // <- can now optimize to 0
}
```
If we know where we need optimizations, can control the reference creation, and are fine being a bit verbose, then this could help.

