Ugh damn, I realised this probably isn't going to work after all... Field projections generalises reading to something like:

```rust
impl ReadPlace: PlaceProxy {
  fn read_place(self) -> <Self as PlaceProxy>::Target;
}
```

The most basic implementation would internally do something like `ptr::read(self.0)` on a `*const/mut Self::Target` - so field projection (FP) read will already do a retag and therefore invalidate existing shared references. So I was actually totally wrong: I cannot rely on FP's read logic mostly probably.

