Consider this Rust code: [(playground)](https://play.rust-lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=9f9d968d3ae741379e00760b8b36bab6)

```rust
struct Foo {
    x: i32,
    y: UnsafeCell<i32>
}

fn foo(x : &mut Foo) {
    std::alloc::dealloc(x as *mut _ as *mut u8, Layout::new::<Foo>());
}

fn main() {
    let x : *mut Foo = std::alloc::alloc(Layout::new::<Foo>()) as *mut _;
    (*x).x = 42;
    (*x).y = UnsafeCell::new(42);
    foo(&mut *x);
}
```

This code has UB under both Stacked and Tree Borrows. But the reference [says](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/behavior-considered-undefined.html#r-undefined.alias):

```quote
* When a reference (but not a `Box`!) is passed to a function, it is live at least as long as that function call, again **except if the `&T` contains an [`UnsafeCell<U>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/core/cell/struct.UnsafeCell.html).**
```

This is wrong, isn't it? It should say "except if all bytes of T are in an `UnsafeCell`" or something like that.

